---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Workbench from '../components/Workbench';
import DemoVideo from '../components/DemoVideo.astro';
import { profile, career, projects, experiments, books } from '../data/content';
const categories = [...new Set(projects.map(project => project.discipline))];
---
<Layout title="Aleem Siddique — Engineering, experiments & stories" description="Product Development Engineer at AMD. Explore Aleem Siddique's engineering projects, interactive experiments, and fiction.">
  <section id="workbench" class="workbench-section" data-workbench aria-label="Introduction and creative workbench">
    <div class="hero wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="identity">Product engineer. Curious by nature.</p>
        <h1>Engineering,<br />experiments<br />and stories.</h1>
        <p class="hero-intro">I’m Aleem, a Product Development Engineer at AMD. I bring silicon into the world, build things you can play with, and write worlds you can get lost in.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#work">Explore my work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#experience">Meet the engineer</a></div>
        <div class="scene-selector" aria-label="Focus the creative workbench">
          <button data-workbench-select="lens" aria-pressed="true"><span class="object-dot lens-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Lens</button>
          <button data-workbench-select="circuit" aria-pressed="false"><span class="object-dot circuit-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Circuit</button>
          <button data-workbench-select="book" aria-pressed="false"><span class="object-dot book-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Book</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="workbench-visual">
        <div class="workbench-stage">
          <Workbench client:visible />
          <span class="stage-note">A few tools. Many possibilities.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="scene-caption" aria-live="polite">
          <p data-focus-caption="lens"><strong>Precision, made physical.</strong> The lens connects code to movement. <a href="/work/icm-buddy/">Explore ICM Buddy</a></p>
          <p data-focus-caption="circuit" hidden><strong>Ideas, brought to life.</strong> From silicon bring-up to AI in the browser. <a href="#experience">Explore the engineering</a></p>
          <p data-focus-caption="book" hidden><strong>Another kind of worldbuilding.</strong> Stories about identity, relationships and imagined worlds. <a href="#writing">Explore the stories</a></p>
          <span class="scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">Scroll to explore <span>↓</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="experience" class="experience-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
    <div class="wrap experience-grid">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="section-kicker">The day job</p><h2 id="experience-title">Bringing silicon<br />into the world.</h2><p class="section-deck">Good engineering lives in the details—and in the trade-offs you find a way through.</p></div>
      <div class="career-story">
        <div class="career-role"><span class="amd-mark" aria-hidden="true">AMD <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M3 3h14v14h-5V8H3Zm0 8h6v6H3Z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span><div><h3>{career.role}</h3><p>{career.dates}</p></div></div>
        <p>{career.summary}</p>
        <p>Quality and yield can pull in opposite directions. My team and I worked to improve both together, challenging the trade-off through careful product development.</p>
        <ul class="product-list" aria-label="Products contributed to">{career.products.map(product => <li>{product}</li>)}</ul>
        <aside class="recognition"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="44" height="44" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 3 4 5 7-1 1 7 5 4-5 5-1 7-7-1-4 5-5-5-7 1-1-7-5-5 5-4 1-7 7 1Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="m14 19 4 4 8-9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/></svg><div><h3>{career.recognition.title}</h3><p>{career.recognition.detail}</p></div><span>{career.recognition.year}</span></aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="selected-work wrap section-pad" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="section-top"><div><p class="section-kicker">Independent work</p><h2 id="work-title">Built to be explored.</h2></div><p class="section-deck">Physical prototypes, learning systems and interactive worlds. Each starts with a question worth working through.</p></div>
    <div class="work-filters" aria-label="Filter case studies"><button data-project-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All work</button>{categories.map(category => <button data-project-filter={category} aria-pressed="false">{category}</button>)}</div>
    <p class="sr-only" data-filter-status aria-live="polite">{projects.length} projects shown</p>
    <div class="project-grid">
      {projects.map((project, index) => <article class:list={['project-card', { 'project-card-large': index < 2 }]} data-project-category={project.discipline}>
        <a class="project-image" href={`/work/${project.slug}/`} tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src={project.image} alt="" width="1000" height="700" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span class="image-open" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <div class="project-meta"><span>{project.category}</span><span>{project.year}</span></div>
        <h3><a href={`/work/${project.slug}/`}>{project.title}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3><p>{project.summary}</p>
      </article>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="film-section wrap" aria-labelledby="film-title">
    <div class="film-copy"><p class="section-kicker">From idea to movement</p><h2 id="film-title">Make it tangible.</h2><p>A small study in mechanisms, materials and motion. The same curiosity runs through the work.</p></div>
    <figure><DemoVideo mp4="/showcase-assets/media/workbench-render.mp4" webm="/showcase-assets/media/workbench-render.webm" poster="/showcase-assets/media/workbench-poster.webp" label="Creative workbench: lens, circuit and book in motion" /><figcaption>A motion study rendered from the interactive workbench.</figcaption><details class="film-alternate"><summary>See a studio interpretation</summary><DemoVideo mp4="/showcase-assets/media/workbench-film.mp4" webm="/showcase-assets/media/workbench-film.webm" poster="/showcase-assets/media/workbench-film-poster.webp" label="Concept visualization of a camera lens, circuit and book in a light studio" loop={false} /><p>Generated concept visualization.</p></details></figure>
  </section>

  <section id="writing" class="writing-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-top"><div><p class="section-kicker">Away from the circuit board</p><h2 id="writing-title">Some worlds<br />begin with words.</h2></div><div class="writing-intro"><p>Fiction about identity, relationships and imagined worlds—from contemporary Singapore stories to speculative thrillers and fantasy.</p><a class="text-link" href="/novel/">Open the full library <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
      <div class="book-grid">{books.map(book => <article class="book-card"><a class="book-cover" href={book.href} tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src={book.image} alt="" width="480" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><div class="book-copy"><p class="book-genre">{book.genre}</p><h3><a href={book.href}>{book.title}</a></h3><p>{book.description}</p><a class="text-link" href={book.href} aria-label={`Read ${book.title}`}>Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="experiments" class="experiments-section wrap section-pad" aria-labelledby="experiments-title">
    <div class="section-top"><div><p class="section-kicker">The playground</p><h2 id="experiments-title">A little room<br />to experiment.</h2></div><p class="section-deck">Games, quizzes and ideas that became working experiences. Try something; see where it takes you.</p></div>
    <div class="experiment-grid">{experiments.map(experiment => <article class="experiment-card">{experiment.image && <img src={experiment.image} alt="" width="560" height="360" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />}<div class="experiment-copy"><p class="project-meta">{experiment.category}</p><h3><a href={experiment.href} target={experiment.href.startsWith('https') ? '_blank' : undefined} rel={experiment.href.startsWith('https') ? 'noopener noreferrer' : undefined}>{experiment.title}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3><p>{experiment.description}</p><a class="source-link" href={experiment.code} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`View ${experiment.title} source`}>View source</a></div></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section wrap section-pad" aria-labelledby="about-title"><div class="portrait-frame"><img src="/showcase-assets/media/portrait.webp" alt="Aleem Siddique" width="700" height="800" loading="lazy" /></div><div class="about-copy"><p class="section-kicker">A thread through it all</p><h2 id="about-title">Curiosity came first.</h2><p>{profile.about}</p><p class="qualification">{profile.qualification}</p><a class="text-link" href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>

  <section id="contact" class="contact-section section-pad" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><div class="wrap contact-grid"><div><p class="section-kicker">Keep the conversation going</p><h2 id="contact-title">What are you<br />curious about?</h2></div><div class="contact-copy"><p>A project, a story, a question. I’m always interested in a thoughtful conversation.</p><a class="contact-email" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="contact-links"><a href={profile.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a><a href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a><a href="/novel/">Novel library</a></div></div></div></section>
</Layout>
